{"id": "EUVD-2026-80564", "enisaUuid": "f023f30a-e526-3b16-9bff-4f10a4b881be", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nparisc: eisa: Fix infinite loop when parsing invalid IRQ value\n\nWhen an invalid value is passed via the \"eisa_irq_edge=\" kernel\ncommand line parameter (e.g. \"eisa_irq_edge=16,5\"), eisa_irq_setup()\nprints an error message and continues without advancing the current\nposition.  As a result the same invalid value is parsed again and\nagain, causing an infinite loop while the kernel boots.\n\nAdvance to the next comma-separated entry, or stop parsing when there\nis no next entry, before continuing so that the remaining entries are\nprocessed normally.", "datePublished": "2026-09-16T10:32:46", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:55:37", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/68659b627770f3c8d8f578e8ddee78a07d5f1d0e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8640ade22369e248f77fbdd31a9d71b338499eef", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/21f063e3c2b11fb9078ccdfd3b23634313ce4f0c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/62d88e93ef5e1e04041e347945f7d7510eba1797", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bb10d54b74845eb4547baa1b9e908ecd32aa64e1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3e2691eeee83a819125dba3f42c74e1b6730d5cd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/16a62a3f2128b3d86fefc082d8f631becd02bff5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8b585431a16cfb9d8f2955a9fa0787ce3dceb3c2"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89964", "GHSA-w8m9-w285-5x2j"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "125c0163-30da-37dd-8279-d35197a4899d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "2544caba-46d6-3c51-9062-911b9d304945", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1da177e4c3f41524e886b7f1b8a0c1fc7321cac2 <8640ade22369e248f77fbdd31a9d71b338499eef"}, {"id": "312478e4-0457-3a87-8c0e-bc8306cfb8f6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"na